As of November 2023, three new fundraising plates are currently being considered in the [[Michigan Legislature]]: one supporting Michigan's [[4-H]] organizations, another funding [[Sickle cell disease|sickle cell anemia]] research, and a third supporting [[prostate cancer]] prevention.<ref name=":2" />

Legislation was passed in June 2017 to offer an anti-abortion [[Choose Life license plates|Choose Life plate]] in Michigan, but was vetoed by Governor [[Rick Snyder]].<ref>{{cite web |last=Lawler |first=Emily |date=2017-06-30 |title=Gov. Rick Snyder vetoes bill that would have allowed 'choose life' license plates |url=http://www.mlive.com/news/index.ssf/2017/06/gov_rick_snyder_vetoes_bill_th.html |access-date= |website=[[MLive]] |publisher=}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last=Oosting |first=Jonathan |date=2017-06-30 |title=Snyder vetoes 'Choose Life' license plate |url=https://www.detroitnews.com/story/news/politics/2017/06/30/snyder-vetoes-choose-life-license-plate-michigan/103315188/ |access-date=2023-12-03 |website=The Detroit News |language=en-US}}</ref>

